/-!
# Finite operational realization and recognition with multiplicities

Paper `predictive_spectral_geometry`, labels `thm:ncg-operational-realization`,
`prop:ncg-operational-recognition` and `cor:ncg-operational-calibrated-triples`.

## Hilbert–Schmidt matrices of superoperators

A superoperator `Φ : M_Ω(ℂ) → M_Ω(ℂ)` is encoded by its matrix in the Hilbert–Schmidt
orthonormal basis of matrix units, `superMatrix Φ : Matrix (Ω × Ω) (Ω × Ω) ℂ`; `superApply M`
is the superoperator of a matrix `M`.  Composition is matrix multiplication
(`superApply_mul`), and the Hilbert–Schmidt adjoint is the conjugate transpose
(`hsInner_superApply`, `superMatrix_eq_conjTranspose_of_hsAdjoint`).

## Finite operational schemes

`Scheme Ω ι Br` is a finite physical memory `ℂ^Ω` with boundary preparations `prep : ι → M_Ω`,
terminal readouts (effects) `eff : ι → M_Ω` and a finite family `Br` of two-outcome
instruments `(succ β, fail β)`.  `Scheme.IsValid`: densities, effects, completely positive
branches (finite Kraus form, `IsKrausCP`) and normalized instruments
(`Tr(succ β X + fail β X) = Tr X`).

* `Scheme.processAlgebra`: the internal history algebra, the star subalgebra of
  `B(HS(ℂ^Ω))` generated by the Hilbert–Schmidt matrices of all branches (star = HS adjoint).
* `Scheme.readout i j x = Tr(E_i x(ρ_j))`: the boundary readout contexts;
  `Scheme.futureNull`: the contextual future-null ideal of these readouts
  (`contextualFutureNullIdeal`, both `q` and `q^*` tested in every two-sided context).
* `Scheme.sourceSpan = span{ρ_j}`: the diagonal Hilbert–Schmidt source subspace.
* `Scheme.RealizesRep S π`: **the future-separated source representation of `S` is unitarily
  equivalent to `π`**: there are a surjective star homomorphism `θ : A^proc → A` whose kernel is
  exactly the contextual future-null ideal (so `A^proc / N^fut ≅ A`) and a Hilbert–Schmidt
  unitary `T : ℂ^n ≅ span{ρ_j}` with `x(T v) = T(π(θ x) v)` for every internal history `x`.

## Main results

* `realizesRep_of_frame`: the general compression mechanism (preparations forming a
  Hilbert–Schmidt orthonormal frame, perfectly discriminated, every branch and its
  Hilbert–Schmidt adjoint acting on the frame by given matrices `A_γ`, and the algebra
  generated by the `A_γ` unitarily equivalent to `π(A)`).
* `exists_wedderburn_blockForm`: the Wedderburn block form `Wᴴ π(A) W = ⊕_λ M_{n_λ} ⊗ I_{m_λ}`
  of a faithful representation (from `reciprocal_wedderburn`).
* `realizationScheme`: the explicit realization (rank-one Kraus matrix-unit branches
  `realizationScheme_succ_eq_kraus`, dephasing failure branches `realizationScheme_fail_eq`).
* `operational_realization` (`thm:ncg-operational-realization`).
* `frame_data_of_card_eq`, `card_le_of_perfectDiscrimination`, `Scheme.SamePanel`,
  `operational_recognition` (`prop:ncg-operational-recognition`).
* `operational_calibrated_triples` (`cor:ncg-operational-calibrated-triples`).
-/

namespace RenewalGeometry
namespace OperationalRealization

